// Title: Clipboard Access Via OSAScript
// Sigma ID: 7794fa3c-edea-4cff-bec7-267dd4770fd7
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Sohan G (D4rkCiph3r)
// Date: 2023-01-31 | Modified: 2026-05-22
// ATT&CK: collection, execution, T1115, T1059.002
// Description: Detects access to clipboard content via osascript, which may be used for data collection but
//   also occurs in legitimate clipboard utilities and automation scripts
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate clipboard utilities and automation scripts that read or write clipboard content
//   - Developer tools and IDEs that use osascript for clipboard integration
// References:
//   - https://www.sentinelone.com/blog/how-offensive-actors-use-applescript-for-attacking-macos/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/macos/process_creation/proc_creation_macos_clipboard_access_via_osascript.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "/osascript" and (ProcessCommandLine contains " -e " and ProcessCommandLine contains "clipboard")) and (not((InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "opencode" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "osascript" and ProcessCommandLine contains " -e " and ProcessCommandLine contains "set imageData to the clipboard" and ProcessCommandLine contains "set fileRef"))))
